    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Â©FAO. Editorial use only. Photo credit must be given.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:rights>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">25 May 2017, Ndavaya, Kwale county, Kenya - Marunga Tsuma Joto, 52, ploughing his land with four of his remaining bulls which he managed to save from a decimating drought thanks to a collaborative drought intevention programe led by the Food and Agriculture Organisation's (FAO) known as 'Early Warning, Early Action' (EWEA) that provided fortified feed to mitigate drought at his home village.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
